meta {
  name: submissions - login alice
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

get {
  url: {{bff_url}}/api/auth/login?provider=dev&user=alice
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  The catalog-submissions flow starts here and drives three fixtures
  through one cookie jar: every role switch below (alice, admin, bob,
  admin again) is a re-login that replaces the session the jar holds.
  Run task grant-fixture-admin before the folder so the admin logins
  land the granted role in their JWT.

  A clean run leaves zero residue: alice's and bob's entries are
  deleted at the end (which removes their submission rows with them),
  and the three minted products are guarded-deleted once unreferenced.
  A mid-run abort can leave the fixed-name community product "Bruno
  Community Cart" behind - delete it via the admin lookup, or re-run
  the cleanup legs, before the next run.
}
